# Browser
# What a player sees of banding as the attacker (CR 702.22c, 702.22k): Bot1 declares Benalish Hero and Guerrilla Gorilla and
# is asked, of the Hero, which attackers band with it - the dock says so - and bands the Gorilla; both cards then say BAND 1.
# Bot2's Ulvenwald Oddity blocks the Hero and so blocks the band (CR 702.22h). In the damage step Bot1, not Bot2, divides the
# Oddity's 4 among the band, the dock titled for the opponent's creature's damage: all 4 to the Hero, which dies, and the
# Gorilla lives.

[Bot1 Deck]
Plains
Mox Emerald
Mox Ruby
Benalish Hero
Guerrilla Gorilla
Island x14

[Bot2 Deck]
Forest
Black Lotus
Ulvenwald Oddity
Island x14

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Plains.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Plains.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Benalish Hero.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Guerrilla Gorilla.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot2.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Green)
Bot2.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Ulvenwald Oddity.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Attack(Benalish Hero > Bot2; Guerrilla Gorilla > Bot2)
? Client.Bot1.Prompt.Title = Benalish Hero has banding: choose attacking creatures to band with it, or none
Bot1.Choose(Guerrilla Gorilla)
? Client.Bot1.Confirm = Band with it
? Client.Bot1.Battlefield.Benalish Hero.Status = BAND 1
? Client.Bot1.Battlefield.Guerrilla Gorilla.Status = BAND 1
Bot2.Block(Ulvenwald Oddity > Benalish Hero)
[T3 Bot1.Blockers]
Bot1.Pass
? Client.Bot1.Prompt.Title = Banding: divide their creature's combat damage
Bot1.AssignDamage(Ulvenwald Oddity > Benalish Hero: 4)
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Turn = 3
Bot2.Life = 20
Bot1.Graveyard = Benalish Hero
Bot1.Battlefield.Guerrilla Gorilla.Damage = 0
Bot2.Battlefield.Ulvenwald Oddity.Damage = 3
